:: Home Console Pet
<<set $outside to 0>>
<<if $location isnot "home" and $location isnot "alex_cottage">><<set $location to "home">><</if>>
<<effects>>
<<set _ret to ($location is "alex_cottage" ? "Farm Bedroom" : "Bedroom")>>
<<furnitureicon "controller">>You open the virtual pet game.
<br><br>
<<run Tamagotchi.sync()>>
<<if not Tamagotchi.exists()>>
	A small egg covered in coloured spots appears on the screen. It shakes, cracks open, and reveals the list of pets you can start with.
	<br><br>
	What will you name it?
	<br>
	<<textbox "_petname" "Pixel">>
	<br><br>
	<div class="pa-picks"><<for _sp range Tamagotchi.listSpecies()>><<capture _sp>><div class="pa-pick"><<= PetArt.pick(_sp.id)>><div class="pa-pick-text"><span class="pa-pick-head"><span class="pa-pick-name"><<print _sp.name>></span> <span class="pa-pick-type teal"><<print _sp.typeLabel>> type</span></span><span class="pa-pick-blurb"><<print _sp.blurb>></span><span class="pa-pick-choose"><<link [["Choose " + _sp.name|Home Console Pet]]>><<run setup.consoleSfx.play("pet-select")>><<run Tamagotchi.hatch(_petname, _sp.id)>><</link>></span></div></div><</capture>><</for>></div>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Back to the console|Home Console]]>><</link>>
	<br>

<<elseif not Tamagotchi.isAlive()>>
	<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
	The screen shows a small headstone with <span class="blue">_t.name</span>'s name on it.
	<<if _t.deathCause is "battle">>
		Your pet was defeated in battle and did not survive.
	<<elseif _t.deathCause is "boss">>
		The blood-moon boss attacked while you were away. You never returned to fight it before it reached _t.name.
	<<elseif _t.deathCause is "abandoned">>
		An enemy attacked while you were away, and you did not return in time to defend _t.name.
	<<elseif _t.deathCause is "illness">>
		_t.name became sick and died before receiving medicine.
	<<else>>
		_t.name went without food and care for too long.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Your hand stays still on the console while you read the cause of death again, remembering the time you spent feeding, playing with, and training _t.name. You look back at its name on the headstone and wish you could go back and keep it alive.<<stress 9>><<ggstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _t.elixirs gt 0>>
		<span class="green">You have _t.elixirs <<= _t.elixirs is 1 ? "Elixir" : "Elixirs">> from Robin. You could use one to bring <span class="blue">_t.name</span> back.</span>
		<br>
		<<link [[Use an Elixir to revive it|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.reviveWithElixir()>><<run setup.consoleSfx.play("pet-cure")>><</link>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _t.backupAlive>>
		<span class="green">One of your other pets is still with you.</span>
		<br>
		<<for _p range _t.backups>>
			<<if _p.alive>>
				<<capture _p>>
					<<link [["Continue with " + _p.name|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.promoteBackup(_p.index)>><</link>>
				<</capture>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Lay them to rest and start over|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.bury()>><</link>><<if _t.backupAlive>> <span class="red">(this buries your living pets too!)</span><</if>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Back to the console|Home Console]]>><</link>>

<<else>>
	<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
	<<if Tamagotchi.ackWoke()>>
		<<= _t.name>> has woken from its nap. Its energy is restored, but <span class="green">it is very hungry, and it has left a mess</span> for you to clean.
		<br>
	<</if>>
	You check in on <span class="blue">_t.name</span>.
	<<if _t.sleeping>> <span class="teal">It's fast asleep.</span><</if>>
	<<if _t.sick>> <span class="red">It looks ill.</span><</if>>
	<<if _t.poops gt 0>> There <<= _t.poops is 1 ? "is a mess" : "are messes">> on the screen that <<= _t.poops is 1 ? "needs" : "need">> cleaning.<</if>>
	<br>

	<<= Tamagotchi.statusHtml()>>

	<<if _t.bossDue>>
		A monstrous boss has appeared under the blood moon and is coming after <<= _t.name>>!
		You have _t.bossDaysLeft <<= _t.bossDaysLeft is 1 ? "day" : "days">> to defeat it. If you leave it alone after that, <span class="red">the boss will kill your pet</span>.
		<<if _t.backupAlive>>
			<br>One of your other living pets is ready to help. If <<= _t.name>> is defeated, <span class="green">that pet will take its place in the battle</span>.
		<</if>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Face the boss!|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.startWeeklyBattle()>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _t.pendingAttack and not _t.bossDue>>
		An enemy is attacking <<= _t.name>> right now! <span class="red">You have to defend it</span>!
		<<if _t.backupAlive>>
			<br>One of your other living pets is ready to help. If <<= _t.name>> is defeated, <span class="green">that pet will take its place in the battle</span>.
		<</if>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Defend your pet!|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.startWeeklyBattle()>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br><br>
		<<link "Step away (risky)" _ret>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><</link>>
	<<elseif _t.sleeping>>
		<<= _t.name>> is curled up asleep and <span class="teal">can't be disturbed</span> for about _t.sleepHoursLeft
		<<= _t.sleepHoursLeft is 1 ? "hour" : "hours">>. Come back once it's rested.
		<br><br>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Back to the console|Home Console]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<if _t.pendingSkillChoice>>
			<<= _t.name>> has completed the training needed to <span class="gold">learn a new skill</span>!
			<br>
			<<link [[Choose a new skill|Home Console Pet Skill Pick]]>><</link>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<span class="small-description"><i>The next challenger will arrive in about _t.nextAttackDays
			<<= _t.nextAttackDays is 1 ? "day" : "days">>.</i></span>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<if _t.canEvolve>>
			<<= _t.name>> is ready to evolve.
			Evolving will make it much stronger, but <span class="gold">_t.evolveCost of its learned skills will be permanently removed</span>.
			<br>
			<<link [[Evolve your pet|Home Console Pet Evolve]]>><</link>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		/* Care and activities as tiles. A tile the pet needs right now gets a gold edge and says why in words. */
		<h3 class="pet-menu-head">Care</h3>
		<div class="pet-tiles">
			<div @class="'pet-tile' + (_t.hunger gte 50 ? ' pet-tile--need' : '')"><<icon "food/eat.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Feed it|Home Console Do]]>><<set $consoleAction to "feed">><<pass 5>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">0:05<<if _t.hunger gte 50>> · <span class="gold">_t.hungerWord</span><</if>></span></span></div>
			<div @class="'pet-tile' + (_t.happiness lte 50 ? ' pet-tile--need' : '')"><<icon "balloons.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Play with it|Home Console Do]]>><<set $consoleAction to "play">><<pass 15>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">0:15<<if _t.happiness lte 50>> · <span class="gold">_t.happinessWord</span><</if>></span></span></div>
			<<if _t.poops gt 0>>
				<div class="pet-tile pet-tile--need"><<icon "broom-dustpan.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Clean up the mess|Home Console Do]]>><<set $consoleAction to "clean">><<pass 5>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">0:05 · <span class="gold"><<= _t.poops is 1 ? "1 mess" : _t.poops + " messes">></span></span></span></div>
			<</if>>
			<<if _t.sick>>
				<div class="pet-tile pet-tile--need"><<icon "pill.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Give it medicine|Home Console Do]]>><<set $consoleAction to "cure">><<pass 5>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">0:05 · <span class="gold">Ill</span></span></span></div>
			<</if>>
			<div @class="'pet-tile' + (_t.energy lte 40 ? ' pet-tile--need' : '')"><<icon "zzz.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Let it sleep|Home Console Do]]>><<set $consoleAction to "rest">><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">Sleeps 6 hours<<if _t.energy lte 40>> · <span class="gold">_t.energyWord</span><</if>></span></span></div>
		</div>
		<h3 class="pet-menu-head">Activities</h3>
		<div class="pet-tiles">
			/* Training shows only when the pet can train; otherwise the option is simply not offered today. */
			<<set _ct to Tamagotchi.canTrain()>>
			<<if _ct.ok>>
				<div class="pet-tile"><<icon "physique.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Train your pet|Home Console Pet Train]]>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">Once a day</span></span></div>
			<</if>>
			<<set _petBattleNow to Tamagotchi.battleState()>>
			<<if _petBattleNow and _petBattleNow.kind is "challenge">>
				<div class="pet-tile pet-tile--need"><<icon "target.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Return to your challenge battle|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta gold">In progress</span></span></div>
			<<else>>
				<<set _pcProg to setup.petChallenges.progress()>>
				<<set _pcDaily to setup.petChallenges.dailyView()>>
				<div class="pet-tile"><<icon "target.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Challenges and daily battle|Home Console Pet Challenges]]>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta"><<print _pcProg.count>> of <<print _pcProg.total>> done · <<if _pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.done>>today's battle won<<elseif _pcDaily.c.reward>>today's battle pays <<print formatMoney(_pcDaily.c.reward)>><<else>>today's battle open<</if>></span></span></div>
			<</if>>
			<<if _t.inDungeon>>
				<div class="pet-tile pet-tile--need"><<icon "key-iron.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Resume your dungeon run|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta gold">In progress</span></span></div>
			<<elseif _t.keys gt 0>>
				<div class="pet-tile"><<icon "key-iron.png" "nowhitespace">><span class="pet-tile-text"><<link [[Enter the dungeon|Home Console Dungeon Enter]]>><</link>><span class="pet-tile-meta">_t.keys <<= _t.keys is 1 ? "key" : "keys">></span></span></div>
			<</if>>
		</div>
		<<if _t.hasBackup>>
			<span class="small-description"><i>Your other pets:</i></span>
			<br>
			<<for _p range _t.backups>>
				<<capture _p>>
					<<if _p.alive>>
						<span class="tama-bench-pet"><<= PetArt.icon(_p.species)>><span class="blue">_p.name</span></span> <span class="teal">(_p.typeLabel)</span><<if _p.atCap>> <span class="gold">(maxed)</span><</if>><<if _p.needsCare>> <span class="red">(needs care)</span><</if>>
						<br>
						<<link [["Switch to " + _p.name|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.switchActive(_p.index)>><</link>>
					<<else>>
						<span class="red">_p.name <span class="teal">(_p.typeLabel)</span> has passed away.</span>
						<<if _t.elixirs gt 0>>
							<br>
							<<link [["Use an Elixir to revive " + _p.name|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.reviveBackupWithElixir(_p.index)>><</link>>
						<</if>>
					<</if>>
				<</capture>>
				<br>
			<</for>>
			<<if _t.backupCount gt _t.backupAliveCount>>
				<<link [[Lay dead pets to rest|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.buryDeadBackups()>><</link>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if _t.canAdopt>>
			You can <span class="gold">add another elemental pet</span> to your collection. Every living pet you already have has reached its current maximum strength.
			<br>
			<<link [[Adopt another pet|Home Console Pet Adopt]]>><</link>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif _t.collectionComplete and _t.atCap>>
			<<= _t.name>> <span class="gold">cannot grow any stronger</span>, and your collection already contains pets from all four elements.
			<br><br>
		<<elseif _t.atCap and _t.adoptableCount gt 0>>
			<<= _t.name>> <span class="gold">cannot grow any stronger</span>.
			To adopt another elemental pet, every other living pet in your collection must also reach its maximum strength.
			<br><br>
		<<elseif _t.adoptableCount gt 0 and _t.capMissingText>>
			<span class="small-description"><i>You can adopt another elemental pet after this pet reaches the maximum value for every stat. It still needs: <<= _t.capMissingText>>.</i></span>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<<= setup.consoleSfx.controlsHtml()>>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Back to the console|Home Console]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Do
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _ret to ($location is "alex_cottage" ? "Farm Bedroom" : "Bedroom")>>

<<set _action to $consoleAction>><<unset $consoleAction>>
<<switch _action>>
	<<case "feed">><<set _result to Tamagotchi.feed()>>
	<<case "play">><<set _result to Tamagotchi.play()>>
	<<case "clean">><<set _result to Tamagotchi.clean()>>
	<<case "cure">><<set _result to Tamagotchi.cure()>>
	<<case "rest">><<set _result to Tamagotchi.rest()>>
	<<default>><<set _result to "invalid">>
<</switch>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
/* A sound only for an action that happened; refusals (too tired, already clean...) stay silent. */
<<run setup.consoleSfx.play({ fed: "pet-feed", played: "pet-play", cleaned: "pet-clean", sleeping: "pet-sleep", cured: "pet-cure" }[_result])>>

<<switch _result>>
	<<case "fed">>
		You give <span class="blue">_t.name</span> some food. It walks over and eats quickly until the food is gone.
	<<case "overfed">>
		You offer <span class="blue">_t.name</span> more food, but it steps away and refuses to eat. It's already full.
	<<case "played">>
		You start a quick minigame with <span class="blue">_t.name</span>. It follows your commands until the game ends, then jumps up and down on the screen.<<stress -10>><<lstress>>
	<<case "tooTired">>
		<span class="blue">_t.name</span> is too tired to play. It needs to rest first.
	<<case "cleaned">>
		You clear the mess from <span class="blue">_t.name</span>'s area. Once the floor is clean again, it walks back across the screen without avoiding the dirty spots.
	<<case "alreadyClean">>
		There's nothing to clean.
	<<case "sleeping">>
		You tell <span class="blue">_t.name</span> to rest. It lies down, closes its eyes, and goes to sleep. It'll nap for about 6 hours and can't be disturbed until it wakes.
	<<case "alreadyAsleep">>
		<span class="blue">_t.name</span> is already fast asleep.
	<<case "asleep">>
		<span class="blue">_t.name</span> is asleep and can't be disturbed right now.
	<<case "cured">>
		You give <span class="blue">_t.name</span> some medicine. After a short pause, the sick status disappears and it starts moving normally again.
	<<case "notSick">>
		<span class="blue">_t.name</span> isn't sick.
	<<case "dead">>
		The game only shows your pet's death screen. None of the normal care options can help it now.
	<<default>>
		You press a few buttons, but nothing useful happens.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>


:: Home Console Pet Train
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>

<<set _ct to Tamagotchi.canTrain()>>
<<if not _ct.ok>>
	You can't train right now| <i>_ct.reason</i>.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	How will you train <span class="blue">_t.name</span> today? It can train once per day.
	<br><br>
	<<for _tr range Tamagotchi.trainingTypes()>>
		<<capture _tr>>
			<<link [[_tr.name (1:30)|Home Console Pet Train Do]]>><<set $trainType to _tr.id>><<pass 90>><</link>>
		<</capture>>
		| <i>_tr.desc</i>
		<br>
	<</for>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Home Console Pet Train Do
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>

<<set _trainType to $trainType>><<unset $trainType>>
<<set _r to Tamagotchi.train(_trainType)>>
<<if not _r.ok>>
	You can't train right now| <i>_r.reason</i>.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
	<<run setup.consoleSfx.play(_r.unlocked ? "pet-levelup" : "pet-train")>>
	<<switch _r.type>>
		<<case "strength">>
			You have <span class="blue">_t.name</span> strike a row of small training blocks. Its first hits barely move them, but it keeps trying until one breaks. By the end of the session, each hit lands harder than the first.
		<<case "endurance">>
			You have <span class="blue">_t.name</span> run repeated laps around the training track. Its pace slows near the end, but it finishes every lap before stopping to rest.
		<<case "agility">>
			You guide <span class="blue">_t.name</span> through an obstacle course several times. It bumps into a few obstacles at first, then starts turning sooner and finishing the course faster.
		<<case "defense">>
			You have <span class="blue">_t.name</span> practise blocking repeated attacks. At first it raises its guard too late, but after several tries it starts blocking before each hit reaches it.
		<<case "focus">>
			You have <span class="blue">_t.name</span> sit still for a focus exercise. It keeps breaking concentration at first, but after several tries it remains still until the exercise ends.
		<<default>>
			<span class="blue">_t.name</span> finishes its training session.
	<</switch>>
	<<= " <span class='green'>(+" + _r.gain + " " + _r.stat + ")</span>">>
	<br><br>
	<<if _r.unlocked>>
		<<= _t.name>> has completed the training needed to <span class="gold">learn a new skill</span>!
		<br>
		<<link [[Choose a new skill|Home Console Pet Skill Pick]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Pet Skill Pick
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
<<set _offer to Tamagotchi.skillOfferList()>>

<<if _offer.length is 0>>
	There's no new skill to choose right now.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	Choose a new skill for <span class="blue">_t.name</span>. You can pick one:
	<br><br>
	<<for _s range _offer>>
		<<capture _s>>
			<<link [[_s.name|Home Console Pet]]>><<run Tamagotchi.chooseSkill(_s.id)>><<run setup.consoleSfx.play("pet-levelup")>><</link>>
		<</capture>>
		| <span class="teal">_s.typeLabel</span><<if _s.passive>>, passive | Revives once per battle<<elseif _s.heal>>, restores HP, _s.mp MP<<else>>, Power _s.power, _s.mp MP<</if>>
		<br>
	<</for>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Pet Battle
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _b to Tamagotchi.battleState()>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>

<<if _b is null>>
	The battle is over.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set _petChal to setup.petChallenges.status(_b)>>
	<<if _petChal>>
		<div class="con-banner pet-goal" role="status"><div class="con-daily-head"><strong><<print _petChal.c.name>></strong><<print setup.petChallenges.chip(_petChal.c.diff)>></div><<print setup.petChallenges.describe(_petChal.c)>><<if _petChal.text>><div class="tama-sub"><<print _petChal.text>></div><</if>><<if _petChal.broken>><div class="red">Challenge missed: <<print _petChal.broken>>. You can still finish the fight.</div><</if>></div>
	<</if>>
	<<= PetArt.battleStage()>>
	<div class="pa-after">
	<div class="tama-log">
	<<for _line range _b.log>>
		_line<br>
	<</for>>
	</div>

	<<if _b.over>>
		<<link [[Continue|Home Console Pet Battle Result]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		Your move:
		<br>
		<<link [[Attack|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.battleAttack()>><</link>> <i>(basic, free)</i>
		<br>
		<<link [[Guard|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.battleGuard()>><</link>> <i>(halve next hit, recover MP)</i>
		<br>
		<<link [[Rest|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.battleRest()>><</link>> <i>(recover HP &amp; MP)</i>
		<br>
		<<if _t.autoRevive and not _b.reviveUsed>>
			<i><span class="green">Revive is ready</span>: your pet will get back up once if it falls this battle.</i>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<for _s range Tamagotchi.battleSkills()>>
			<<capture _s>>
				<<if _b.mp gte _s.mp>>
					<<link [[_s.name|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.battleSkill(_s.id)>><</link>>
				<<else>>
					<span class="grey">_s.name</span>
				<</if>>
			<</capture>>
			| <span class="teal">_s.typeLabel</span><<if _s.heal>>, heal<<else>>, Pow _s.power<</if>>, _s.mp MP
			<br>
		<</for>>
	<</if>>
	</div>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Pet Battle Result
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<if Tamagotchi.battleState() and Tamagotchi.battleState().kind is "challenge">>
	/* A challenge battle ends here, not through endBattle(): the pet's own data is never touched. */
	<<set _chalEnd to setup.petChallenges.finish()>>
	<<if _chalEnd.done>>
		<span class="green">Challenge complete: <<print _chalEnd.name>>!</span> Your pet won in <<print _chalEnd.turns>> <<= _chalEnd.turns is 1 ? "turn" : "turns">>.<<stress -4>><<lstress>>
		<<if _chalEnd.paid>><br><span class="gold">You earned <<print formatMoney(_chalEnd.paid)>>.</span><</if>>
		<<if _chalEnd.feat>><br><span class="gold">Every challenge complete. Feat earned: <<print _chalEnd.feat>>.</span><</if>>
	<<elseif _chalEnd.result is "win">>
		Your pet won the fight, but the challenge was missed: <<print _chalEnd.why>>.
	<<else>>
		Your pet is knocked out of the challenge. It is only a practice bout, so it shakes itself off, unhurt.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back to the challenges|Home Console Pet Challenges]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
<<set _sum to Tamagotchi.endBattle()>>

<<if _sum.result is "win">>
	<<if _sum.boss>>
		Your pet lands the final hit on the <span class="green"><<= _sum.enemy>></span>, and the boss falls.<<stress -10>><<lllstress>>
		<br>The blood-moon boss is defeated. Your pet is <span class="green">safe from it for the rest of this month</span>.
	<<elseif _sum.keyGained>>
		Your pet defeats the <span class="green"><<= _sum.enemy>></span> and remains standing after the fight.<<stress -8>><<llstress>>
		<br>The game awards you <span class="gold">a dungeon key</span>. You now hold <<= _sum.keys>>.
	<<elseif _sum.dungeon>>
		Your pet defeats the <span class="green"><<= _sum.enemy>></span> blocking the way deeper into the dungeon.<<stress -4>><<lstress>>
	<<else>>
		Your pet defeats the wild <span class="green"><<= _sum.enemy>></span> and survives the attack.<<stress -8>><<llstress>>
		<br>It is safe for now. <span class="green">The next weekly challenger will be stronger</span>.
	<</if>>
	<<if _sum.teammateRevived>>
		<br>The teammate that was defeated during the fight gets back up afterward. It is exhausted, but <span class="green">it survived</span>.
	<</if>>
	<<if _sum.statBoost>>
		<br>
		<span class="gold">Victory has made it stronger!
		<<= "(+" + _sum.hpBoost + " max HP, +" + _sum.statBoost + " to ATK, DEF, SPD and max MP)">></span>
	<</if>>
	<<if _sum.capped>>
		<br>Its stats have reached their maximum values. <span class="gold">Further victories will not increase them</span>.
	<</if>>
<<elseif _sum.result is "lose">>
	The <span class="purple"><<= _sum.enemy>></span> lands the final hit. Your pet falls, and the battle ends before it can get back up. <span class="red">It didn't survive.</span><<stress 6>><<gstress>>
<<else>>
	The battle ends.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _sum.dungeon and _sum.result is "win">>
	<<run Tamagotchi.dungeonMobCleared()>>
	<<link [[Press on|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if _sum.dungeon>><<run Tamagotchi.dungeonEnd()>><</if>>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Pet Evolve
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
<<if $evoPick is undefined>><<set $evoPick to []>><</if>>
<<if not _t.canEvolve>>
	<<= _t.name>> can't evolve right now.
	<<unset $evoPick>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<span class="blue">_t.name</span> is ready to evolve. Evolution will multiply every stat by ten, but the process permanently removes <span class="red">_t.evolveCost learned skills</span>. Choose which skills you want to lose.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold"><<= $evoPick.length>> / _t.evolveCost selected.</span>
	<br>
	<<for _s range Tamagotchi.learnedSkills()>>
		<<capture _s>>
			<<if $evoPick.includes(_s.id)>>
				<<link [[(x) _s.name|Home Console Pet Evolve]]>><<set $evoPick to $evoPick.filter(id => id !== _s.id)>><</link>> <span class="red">to be sacrificed</span>
			<<elseif $evoPick.length lt _t.evolveCost>>
				<<link [[( ) _s.name|Home Console Pet Evolve]]>><<run $evoPick.push(_s.id)>><</link>>
			<<else>>
				<span class="grey">( ) _s.name</span>
			<</if>>
			| <span class="teal">_s.typeLabel</span><<if _s.passive>>, passive<<elseif _s.heal>>, heal<<else>>, Pow _s.power<</if>>
		<</capture>>
		<br>
	<</for>>
	<br>
	<<if $evoPick.length is _t.evolveCost>>
		<<link [[Evolve!|Home Console Pet Evolve Do]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<span class="grey">Select exactly _t.evolveCost skills to evolve.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Cancel|Home Console Pet]]>><<unset $evoPick>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Pet Evolve Do
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _evo to Tamagotchi.evolve($evoPick)>>
<<unset $evoPick>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>

<<if not _evo or not _evo.ok>>
	Nothing happens.
<<else>>
	<<= PetArt.evolution()>>
	You sacrifice <span class="red"><<= _evo.sacrificed.join(", ")>></span>.
	<br>

	The evolution animation begins. <span class="blue">_t.name</span>'s image flashes several times before changing into its new form.
	<span class="blue">_t.name</span> has evolved from <span class="teal"><<= _evo.from>></span> into <span class="gold"><<= _evo.to>></span>!
	<<stress -10>><<lllstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<= Tamagotchi.statusHtml()>>
	<<if _evo.capped>>
		<br><<= _t.name>> is already <span class="gold">as strong as it can ever be</span>.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>

:: Home Console Pet Adopt
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
<<set _adoptable to Tamagotchi.adoptableSpecies()>>
<<if not _t.canAdopt or _adoptable.length is 0>>
	You can't adopt another pet right now.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	A new egg appears beside your other pets. The game only offers elements that are still missing from your collection. Choose a species, then give the new pet a name.
	<br>
	<<textbox "_petname" "Pixel">>
	<br><br>
	<div class="pa-picks"><<for _sp range _adoptable>><<capture _sp>><div class="pa-pick"><<= PetArt.pick(_sp.id)>><div class="pa-pick-text"><span class="pa-pick-head"><span class="pa-pick-name"><<print _sp.name>></span> <span class="pa-pick-type teal"><<print _sp.typeLabel>> type</span></span><span class="pa-pick-blurb"><<print _sp.blurb>></span><span class="pa-pick-choose"><<link [["Choose " + _sp.name|Home Console Pet]]>><<run setup.consoleSfx.play("pet-select")>><<run Tamagotchi.adopt(_petname, _sp.id)>><</link>></span></div></div><</capture>><</for>></div>
	<br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Pet Challenges
<<set $outside to 0>>
<<if $location isnot "home" and $location isnot "alex_cottage">><<set $location to "home">><</if>>
<<effects>>
<<run Tamagotchi.sync()>>
<<furnitureicon "controller">>Practice bouts for your pet. Each opponent is matched to your pet's current strength, and a lost bout costs nothing: your pet can't be hurt, and it gains no stats from winning.
<br><br>
<<set _pcBlock to setup.petChallenges.blocked()>>
<<set _pcBattle to Tamagotchi.battleState()>>
<<if _pcBattle and _pcBattle.kind is "challenge">>
	<span class="gold">A challenge battle is still under way.</span>
	<br>
	<<link [[Return to it|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><</link>>
	<br><br>
<<elseif _pcBlock>>
	<span class="red"><<print _pcBlock>></span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set _pcDaily to setup.petChallenges.dailyView()>>
<div class="con-list">
<section @class="'con-daily' + (_pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.done ? ' con-daily--done' : '')" aria-label="Today's battle"><div class="con-daily-head"><span class="con-daily-date">Today's battle, <<print _pcDaily.c.date>> (UTC)</span><<print _pcDaily.chip>></div><<if _pcDaily.art>><div class="con-vs"><span class="con-vs-side"><<print _pcDaily.petArt>><span class="con-vs-name"><<print $tamagotchi.name>></span></span><span class="con-vs-word">vs</span><span class="con-vs-side"><<print _pcDaily.art>><span class="con-vs-name"><<print _pcDaily.foeName>></span></span></div><</if>><p class="con-daily-goal"><<print _pcDaily.describe>></p><dl class="con-facts"><dt>Opponent</dt><dd><<print _pcDaily.foe>></dd><dt>Reward</dt><dd><<print _pcDaily.reward>></dd><dt>Status</dt><dd><<if _pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.done>><span class="green">Completed</span><<elseif _pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.tries>>Not completed yet<<else>>Not tried yet<</if>></dd><dt>Best</dt><dd><<if _pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.best isnot null and _pcDaily.rec.best isnot undefined>>Won in <<print _pcDaily.rec.best>> turns<<else>>None yet<</if>><<if _pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.tries>>, <<print _pcDaily.rec.tries>> <<= _pcDaily.rec.tries is 1 ? "try" : "tries">><</if>></dd><dt>Next battle</dt><dd>in <<print _pcDaily.reset>> (midnight UTC)</dd></dl><<if !_pcBlock and !_pcBattle>><span class="pet-chal-start con-btn-link"><<link `_pcDaily.rec and _pcDaily.rec.tries ? "Retry today's battle (0:05)" : "Fight today's battle (0:05)"` "Home Console Pet Battle">><<run setup.petChallenges.start("daily")>><<pass 5>><</link>></span><</if>></section>
<<print _pcDaily.history>>
<<set _pcProg to setup.petChallenges.progress()>>
<h3 class="con-page-head">Challenges</h3>
<div class="con-progress"><div class="con-progress-head"><span>Completed</span><span class="con-progress-count"><<print _pcProg.count>> of <<print _pcProg.total>></span></div><div class="con-bar" role="progressbar" aria-label="Challenges completed" aria-valuemin="0" @aria-valuemax="_pcProg.total" @aria-valuenow="_pcProg.count"><span class="con-bar-fill" @style="'width:' + Math.round(_pcProg.count / _pcProg.total * 100) + '%'"></span></div></div>
<<= setup.petChallenges.featCard()>>
<<set _pcRows to setup.petChallenges.rows()>>
<<for _pcLevel range ["easy", "medium", "hard"]>><<set _pcGroup to _pcRows.filter(r => r.diff is _pcLevel)>><h4 class="con-group-head"><span><<print setup.consoleDaily.levelName(_pcLevel)>></span><span class="con-progress-count"><<print _pcGroup.filter(r => r.done).length>> of <<print _pcGroup.length>></span></h4><<for _pcRow range _pcGroup>><<capture _pcRow>><div @class="'con-row' + (_pcRow.done ? ' con-row--done' : '')"><span class="con-row-icon con-row-icon--pet" aria-hidden="true"><<print _pcRow.art>></span><div class="con-row-main"><span class="con-row-title"><<print _pcRow.name>></span><span class="con-row-desc"><<print _pcRow.describe>></span><span class="con-row-meta">Against <<print _pcRow.foe>>.</span><span class="con-row-status"><<if _pcRow.done>>Completed <<print _pcRow.done>><<elseif _pcRow.needs>><<print _pcRow.needs>><<else>>Not completed<</if>></span></div><div class="con-row-action con-btn-link"><<if !_pcBlock and !_pcBattle and !_pcRow.needs>><<link `_pcRow.done ? "Again" : "Fight"` "Home Console Pet Battle">><<run setup.petChallenges.start(_pcRow.id)>><<pass 5>><</link>><</if>></div></div><</capture>><</for>><</for>>
</div>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back to your pet|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Home Console Dungeon Enter
<<set $outside to 0>><<effects>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>

<<if not Tamagotchi.isAlive() or _t.keys lte 0>>
	You have no keys to open the dungeon.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	A barred gate flickers onto the screen. One of your dungeon keys fits the lock.
	Beyond it lies a crawl of monsters, treasure, and worse.
	<br><br>
	<span class="small-description"><i>A run is 15 tiles deep. You'll find money, items and mobs to grind for stats.
	Falling here is fatal.</i></span>
	<br>
	<<link [[Unlock the gate and descend|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><<pass 1>><<run Tamagotchi.dungeonStart()>><</link>> <i>(1 key)</i>
	<br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Dungeon Walk
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<run Tamagotchi.sync()>>
<<set _d to Tamagotchi.dungeonState()>>

<<if _d is null>>
	You're not inside the dungeon.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<elseif not Tamagotchi.isAlive()>>
	<<run Tamagotchi.dungeonEnd()>>
	The dungeon falls silent.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _d.tile gte _d.tiles>>
	You reach the end of this stretch of the dungeon.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Climb back out|Home Console Dungeon Exit]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	You press deeper into the dungeon. <span class="teal">Tile <<= _d.tile + 1>> of _d.tiles.</span>
	<br>
	<span class="small-description"><i>Found so far: £<<= Math.floor(_d.money / 100)>>,
	_d.items <<= _d.items is 1 ? "item" : "items">>, _d.kills <<= _d.kills is 1 ? "kill" : "kills">>.</i></span>
	<br>
	<<link [[Step deeper|Home Console Dungeon Step]]>><<set $dungeonStep to Tamagotchi.dungeonStep()>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Climb back out|Home Console Dungeon Exit]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Home Console Dungeon Step
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>>
/* $dungeonStep must be a plain story variable: in DoL's SugarCube fork, "$_name" is a widget-local (State.local) that does not survive passage navigation. */
<<set _step to $dungeonStep>><<unset $dungeonStep>>
/* Re-rendering this passage (save load, refresh, history) arrives with $dungeonStep already unset; fall through to the harmless default case instead of crashing the switch below. */
<<if _step is undefined or _step is null>><<set _step to { type: "none" }>><</if>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>

<<switch _step.type>>
	<<case "money">>
		You prise open a mouldering chest and scoop out the coins inside. <<income _step.amount "dungeon">>!
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Continue|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><</link>>
	<<case "item">>
		Tucked in an alcove you find a <span class="green"><<= _step.name>></span>.
		<<if $foodstuff[_step.key] is undefined>><<set $foodstuff[_step.key] to {amount: 0}>><</if>>
		<<set $foodstuff[_step.key].amount += 1>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Continue|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><</link>>
	<<case "mob">>
		A dungeon mob lunges from the shadows!
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Fight!|Home Console Pet Battle]]>><<run Tamagotchi.startDungeonBattle()>><</link>>
	<<case "antipill">>
		Half-buried in the rubble is a single, oddly coloured pill case.
		<br>
		/* Anti-pill / Choice Reversal gift, mirroring Whitney Orphanage Special Event Repeat Finish5. */
		<<set _roll to random(1, 100)>>
		<<set _choiceValid to (V.xchange and V.xchange.pill and V.xchange.pill.choiceEffect)>>
		<<set _choiceKey to "">>
		<<if _choiceValid>>
			<<if V.player.gender is "f">>
				<<set _choiceKey to "X-Change Choice Reversal (M)">>
			<<else>>
				<<set _choiceKey to "X-Change Choice Reversal (F)">>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<<set _antiKeys to ($sexStats and $sexStats.pills and $sexStats.pills.pills) ? Object.keys($sexStats.pills.pills).filter(k => k.startsWith("SWP Anti-") && k.endsWith(" Pill")) : []>>
		<<if _choiceValid and _roll lte 20>>
			<<set _giftKey to _choiceKey>>
		<<elseif _antiKeys.length gt 0>>
			<<set _giftKey to _antiKeys[random(0, _antiKeys.length - 1)]>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _giftKey to _choiceKey>>
		<</if>>
		<<if _giftKey is "" or $sexStats is undefined or $sexStats.pills is undefined>>
			It crumbles to useless dust in your fingers.
		<<else>>
			<<run if (V.sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey] === undefined) V.sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey] = { autoTake: false, doseTaken: 0, owned: 0, overdose: 0 };>>
			<<if $sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey].owned is undefined>><<set $sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey].owned to 0>><</if>>
			<<set $sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey].owned to $sexStats.pills.pills[_giftKey].owned + 1>>
			<<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>>
			<span class="green">It's the <<= _giftKey>>!</span>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Continue|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><</link>>
	<<default>>
		You search around but find nothing...
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Continue|Home Console Dungeon Walk]]>><</link>>
<</switch>>

:: Home Console Dungeon Exit
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<set _d to Tamagotchi.dungeonEnd()>>
You climb back out of the dungeon and switch the game off for now.
<br><br>
<span class="teal">This run you gathered <span class="gold">£<<= Math.floor(_d.money / 100)>></span>,
_d.items <<= _d.items is 1 ? "item" : "items">> and cleared _d.kills <<= _d.kills is 1 ? "mob" : "mobs">>.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Home Console Pet]]>><</link>>
<br>